      en: "Liphofung Cave Monument is an archaeological site in the Lesotho highlands featuring prehistoric San (Bushmen) rock art. The cave also served as a refuge for the Basotho royal family during conflicts. Today it is a protected cultural heritage site, preserving ancient paintings and offering insights into early human habitation.",
