      en: "Bethesda Mission, founded in 1948 by the Dutch Reformed Church, is located near Maseru. The church building is a simple gable-roofed structure. The mission hospital, opened in 1952, now has 100 beds and a renowned eye clinic. The mission provides agricultural extension services and adult education programs. It employs over 200 staff. The hospital treats around 30,000 patients annually. Bethesda is a major provider of healthcare in the Berea district.",
