      en: "St. Luke's Mission in Berea District is one of the oldest mission stations in Lesotho. Founded in 1890 by the Oblate missionaries, the church and associated buildings feature simple neo-Romanesque architecture. The mission played a key role in spreading Christianity and education in the region. Today it houses a school and a health center.",
